# Runtime configuration for deploy/run.sh — copy to .env and fill in.
# These are Azure app registration IDENTIFIERS, not secrets. Safe to keep in
# a file; still git-ignored to allow per-machine values.
#
# As of teams-mcp >= 1.0.x these are RUNTIME env vars (upstream supports them
# natively) — they are no longer baked into the image at build time.
#
# BOTH values are OPTIONAL: with them unset, the server and the CLI both use
# the upstream default (Microsoft Graph CLI app, "common" authority).
#
# ⚠️ The values used by `authenticate.sh` and by the server (run.sh) MUST be
# identical — a refresh token can only be renewed by the client id that
# minted it. If you change these after signing in, run
# `./deploy/run.sh logout` and authenticate again, or the server will report
# "Not authenticated" forever.

# Azure Entra ID app registration: Application (client) ID
# Leave unset to use the upstream default (Graph CLI app).
# Example: 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
#TEAMS_MCP_CLIENT_ID=

# Azure Entra ID: Directory (tenant) ID (GUID or domain name)
# Example GUID:   22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
# Example domain: contoso.onmicrosoft.com
#TEAMS_MCP_TENANT_ID=

# Optional: pin the npm package version instead of "latest"
#TEAMS_MCP_VERSION=1.0.1

# Optional: container timezone
#TZ=US/Mountain
